{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011Cdqf8af3MGq4Afw7CcCuc","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Placement Decision\n\nI would add the new rule as a third bullet point under **\"## 2. Failure handling\"**, immediately after the existing timeout bullet. Here's the edited section:\n\n```markdown\n## 2. Failure handling\n\n- **Retries are bounded and jittered.** Every retry wrapper declares\n  its maximum attempt count at the call site; backoff is exponential\n  with jitter, and a non-retriable error class aborts immediately —\n  enumerate those classes beside the wrapper, not in a distant\n  constants file.\n- **Timeouts are explicit.** No call inherits a library default\n  timeout silently; the call site states its per-attempt timeout.\n- **Wall-clock caps prevent indefinite hangs.** A retry wrapper must\n  cap total elapsed time, not only attempt count — a per-attempt\n  timeout with unbounded attempts still hangs the caller. Declare both\n  the attempt cap and the wall-clock cap at the call site.\n```\n\n**Rationale:** This rule directly extends the timeout guidance by addressing a critical gap (total time bounding) that the previous bullet doesn't cover. It belongs in section 2 since it governs retry/timeout behavior, and placing it after the per-attempt timeout rule creates a logical progression: per-attempt timeouts → total timeouts."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":411,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":299,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}
